></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">r</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⟨</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⟩</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⟨</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⟩</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⟨</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⟩</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace></mstyle><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-71049-e\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">e</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">The plane is undefined</td></tr></tbody></table><div class=\"questionWidget-buttonBar\"><div class=\"questionWidget-submitButton disabledButton\" style=\"display: none;\">Submit</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-spinnerFrame\"><div class=\"questionWidget-spinner\" style=\"display: block;\"></div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-result\"><div class=\"questionWidget-correctIncorrectIcon\"><img src=\"/img/correct-answer.svg\"></div><div class=\"questionWidget-correctText\">Correct</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanation\"><p>First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector <mjx-container class=\"Ma